2026-08-30T10:58Z claude note design input from a corpus look (author's question, 0140 session): 350+ word blocks are mostly extractor artifacts, not authored paragraphs — in 254 sampled PDFs, 58% of 3 939 such blocks carry 2+ sentence-end-newline-capital seams (indentation-separated paragraphs glued when extraction drops the indent), the rest are reference lists and mangled layout; real paragraphs inside run 150-250 words. Consequence for seg/1: when budget-splitting an oversized block, split at those seams rather than at blind token positions — the true boundaries are recoverable; and the weak structure signal is the standing argument for the structured-extraction path (C2) over deeper flat-text heuristics

