--- body ---
## Context
Missing work the implementation review surfaced (§5.1; that review is now
lost -- DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-31 -- and this paragraph is what survives of it):
X5 gates scoped
issue B (0034, which supersedes the RFC 0027) on the segmenter's measured precision, and seg/1
had no implementation anywhere — days of new code standing between 0025's X5
and 0034, priced nowhere until now. The spec lives once, in DESIGN.md §2.2;
build to it, not to a paraphrase. Political-review checkpoint applies: check zotero#6012's state
before building — structured extraction landing upstream makes heuristic
segmentation a fallback at best (political review finding 5, same commit,
panel/cycle2/review-political.md).

## Exit criteria
- [x] #6012 checkpoint recorded here 2026-08-30 — read at source; seg/1 not obsoleted
- [ ] seg/1 runnable over flat /fulltext text of its PRIMARY TARGET CLASS --
      books and proceedings, per the 2026-08-31 ruling (0502 propagated it into
      SPEC.md 5.2.2) -- emitting entries + confidence. The 44,9 MB dictionary is
      the rare case, not the target this criterion is read against; it keeps its
      separate, untouched role as the monster-document RSS fixture (X3a)
- [ ] the primary-class signals built, not the dictionary's: table of contents
      as validator of the cut set, chapter/section numbering, author bylines,
      and page-boundary form feeds where the extraction carries them. The
      headword rhythm/MAD statistic is built only as the dictionary's special
      case, never applied to the primary class
- [ ] deterministic on fixture text; identity string (seg/1) for the chunker key
- [ ] X5 (0025) can consume it on the author's machine: one arm per class,
      scored against each document's embedded outline with the outline tier
      held out, never against the printed contents list (SPEC.md 5.3)
- [ ] the embed path asserts the cap and declares truncation explicitly on the
      call — 0140's action 4, ruled into this bundle (DECISIONS.md
      2026-08-30): the guard ships inside the upstream PR this ticket
      prepares, never as its own filing
